You're working on the ESI.ts project at D:\code\ESI.ts, a TypeScript wrapper for the EVE Online ESI API. We're adopting Zod for runtime response validation.

Your task: Add a `validateResponse` config option that flows through the system.

## Step 1: Add to EsiClientConfig

In `src/EsiClient.ts`, the `EsiClientConfig` interface (around line 65) currently has these fields:
```ts
export interface EsiClientConfig {
  clientId?: string;
  baseUrl?: string;
  accessToken?: string;
  datasource?: EsiDatasource;
  onTokenRefresh?: TokenProvider;
  timeout?: number;
  retryAttempts?: number;
  retryConfig?: RetryConfig;
  enableETagCache?: boolean;
  etagCacheConfig?: ETagCacheConfig;
  enableCircuitBreaker?: boolean;
  circuitBreakerConfig?: CircuitBreakerConfig;
  unsafeAllowCustomHost?: boolean;
  enableRequestDeduplication?: boolean;
  language?: string;
  rateLimiterConfig?: RateLimiterConfig;
  requestInterceptors?: RequestInterceptor[];
  responseInterceptors?: ResponseInterceptor[];
}
```

Add `validateResponse?: boolean;` at the end of the interface. This defaults to true (validation on), but we won't wire it into the request handler yet — that's Phase 4 work.

## Step 2: Add getter/setter to ApiClient

In `src/core/ApiClient.ts`, the `ApiClient` class has private fields and getter/setter pairs for things like cache, rateLimiter, etc.

Add:
- A private field: `private validateResponse: boolean = true;`
- A getter: `getValidateResponse(): boolean { return this.validateResponse; }`
- A setter: `setValidateResponse(validate: boolean): void { this.validateResponse = validate; }`

Add these after the existing `retryConfig` getter/setter pair (around line 83).

## Step 3: Wire in EsiClient constructor

In `src/EsiClient.ts`, in the constructor (starts around line 93), after the existing config wiring (after the interceptors block around line 157), add:

```ts
if (config?.validateResponse !== undefined) {
  this.apiClient.setValidateResponse(config.validateResponse);
}
```

Do NOT modify `src/EsiClientBuilder.ts` — the builder already passes through EsiClientConfig, so it will pick up the new option automatically.

Do NOT touch any other files. This is purely plumbing for now — no validation logic is wired into the request path yet.
